{
  "bridge_text": "那是一个充满好奇的请求，我们就顺着林间细碎的月光，换成你熟悉的语言继续讲吧。风在树梢轻轻摇晃，林娜紧了紧红色的羊毛大衣，在那棵巨大的空心树下屏住了呼吸。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "冬夜的寒风吹得树干呜呜作响，林娜深吸一口气，那低沉的嗡嗡声仿佛在召唤着她。她迈开步子，脚下的积雪发出咯吱咯吱的声响，直到她终于站在了树洞那深不见底的入口前。那里的黑暗里透着一股淡淡的松木香气，那是她从未在村子里闻到过的味道。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While his reasons remain tucked away like shadows, the old fox's gaze lingers on the girl, and the air in the hollow tree grows heavy with his unspoken history. Lina watches him closely as the mystery of his mood stretches out before them.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood her ground, her eyes bright with curiosity. She knew that stories often hide their greatest truths in the places people are told to avoid. The fox watched her, his ears twitching as he weighed her resolve against the silence of the woods."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Mosk the fox stood tall, his vest neatly buttoned as he looked toward the dark stairs, still remembering the name Lina had just whispered.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed firmly at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and offered it as a token for his time. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his eyes softening. Then he stood up, adjusted his green vest, and stepped onto the first stair, silently signaling her to follow him down."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While sneaking might be a clever way to avoid trouble, Lina knew that a simple gift could bridge the distance between two wary souls. She watched as Mosk stood up, finally ready to lead the way.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door, his eyes narrow and watchful. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. Even though she knew she could try to sneak past him, she chose to set the fruit on the step between them. This is for the trouble of walking me down, she said softly. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his stern expression softening just a fraction. He stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The soft moss cradles the firefly as gently as a velvet blanket, keeping her safe in the quiet of the tree. Let us see how Mosk finally makes amends to his old friend.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming deepened into a song, and a firefly the size of a robin rested on a bed of soft, velvet moss. Her glow flickered like a dying candle. Mosk’s whiskers trembled with regret. He remembered a winter long ago when he failed to bring her medicine, and he had been guarding this hollow tree ever since, too ashamed to look her in the eye until this very moment."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The old grey fox named Mosk sat still on the top step, his patched green vest looking dusty in the dim light. Lina waited as he repeated his warning, his voice rustling just like dry autumn leaves.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, Lina discovered a narrow curl of stairs leading deep into the dark. At the very top step sat Mosk, an old grey fox wearing a worn-out green vest. He spoke in a scratchy voice like dry leaves, telling her that the tree was not a place for visitors and that she must return home and forget the strange humming. Lina shook her head, insisting that she could not forget a sound she had not yet truly heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
