{
  "bridge_text": "The shadows in the hollow tree seem to wait with us, holding their breath as the firefly’s light flickers. With that worry tucked away, we watch to see if the warmth returns.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Mosk's whiskers trembled as he remembered that long winter. He had been guarding the tree ever since, too ashamed to face her after failing to bring the medicine. Now, the firefly’s glow pulsed faintly, a heartbeat of light resting on the soft, damp moss."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers. The queen's glow steadied. The humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before — and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
